1
00:05:25,714 --> 00:05:31,714
CLINT EASTWOOD...the deadliest man alive...takes on a whole
army with two guns and a fistful of dynamite!

2
00:10:51,428 --> 00:10:57,428
Two Mules for Sister Sara is a western, adventure,
romance film directed by Don Siegel.

3
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:23,142
When a wandering mercenary named Hogan rescues a nun called Sister Sara from the unwanted attentions of
a band of rogues on the Mexican plains, he has no idea what he has let himself in for.

4
00:21:42,857 --> 00:21:48,857
Their chance encounter results in the blowing up of a train and a French garrison, as
well as igniting a spark between them that survives a shocking discovery.

5
00:27:08,571 --> 00:27:14,571
Sara, played by Shirley MacLaine.

6
00:32:34,285 --> 00:32:40,285
Hogan, played by Clint Eastwood.

7
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Colonel Beltran, played by Manolo Fábregas.

8
00:43:25,714 --> 00:43:31,714
General LeClaire, played by Alberto Morin.

9
00:48:51,428 --> 00:48:57,428
1st American, played by Armando Silvestre.

10
00:54:17,142 --> 00:54:23,142
2nd American, played by John Kelly.

11
00:59:42,857 --> 00:59:48,857
Two Mules for Sister Sara is a 1970 American-Mexican Western film in Panavision directed by Don Siegel and
starring Shirley MacLaine and Clint Eastwood set during the French intervention in Mexico (1861–1867).

12
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
The film was to have been the first in a five-year exclusive association
between Universal Pictures and Sanen Productions of Mexico.

13
01:10:34,285 --> 01:10:40,285
It was the second of five collaborations between Siegel and
Eastwood, following Coogan's Bluff (1968).

14
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The collaboration continued with The Beguiled and Dirty Harry
(both 1971) and finally Escape from Alcatraz (1979).

15
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
The plot follows an American mercenary who gets mixed up with a nun and aids a group of
Juarista rebels during the puppet reign of Emperor Maximilian in Mexico.

16
01:26:51,428 --> 01:26:57,428
The film featured both American and Mexican actors and actresses, including being
filmed in the picturesque countryside near Tlayacapan, Morelos.

17
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
Ennio Morricone composed the film's music.

18
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
Two Mules for Sister Sara was a moderate financial success
and received a warm critical reception.

19
01:43:08,571 --> 01:43:14,571
The film explores themes of gunslinger, brothel, mexican
revolution, treasure hunt, execution.

20
01:48:34,285 --> 01:48:40,285
The tone is emotional.
